        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: செயலிழ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "செயலிழ — ceyaliḻa — \"to stop working; to fail\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "நடுவழியில் எங்கள் காரின் இயந்திரம் செயலிழந்தது. naṭuvaḻiyil eṅkaḷ kāriṉ iyantiram ceyaliḻantatu. Halfway, the engine of our car stopped working."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): செயலிழந்தது, ceyaliḻantatu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "செயல், an action, + இழ, to lose: to lose the power to act. Said of machines and of organs of the body."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "செயலிழ (ceyaliḻa) is built from செயல், \"an action\", the noun of செய், \"to do\" (DEDR 1957), and இழ, \"to lose\" (DEDR 501): to lose the power to act. Like இழ, it makes its past in -ந்த-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
